4,"t":"contest_start","x":"1404: the rebels reach the south.","cp":"glyndwr-s-wales","cpn":"Glyndŵr's Wales","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r","c":1},{"y":1404,"t":"contest_start","x":"1404: Glyndwr's own country.","cp":"glyndwr-s-wales","cpn":"Glyndŵr's Wales","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r","c":1},{"y":1405,"t":"contest_end","x":"May 1405: the rebels lose the south-east.","m":5,"cp":"glyndwr-s-wales","cpn":"Glyndŵr's Wales","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r","c":2},{"y":1407,"t":"contest_end","x":"By 1407: 'the English had recaptured Anglesey and large parts of south Wales'; 'One by one the Lordships began to surrender' after the July 1407 submissions.","cp":"glyndwr-s-wales","cpn":"Glyndŵr's Wales","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glyndwr_Rising","c":2},{"y":1407,"t":"contest_end","x":"1407: 'the superior numbers, resources, and wealth that England had at its disposal began to turn the tide of the war'; by 1409 only 'Harlech and Aberystwyth' were left, so the March is clear of the rebels by 1407-1408; a bridge, confidence 1.","cp":"glyndwr-s-wales","cpn":"Glyndŵr's Wales","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r","c":1},{"y":1536,"t":"dissolve","x":"1536: the Marcher jurisdictions are abolished.","cp":"kingdom-of-england","cpn":"Kingdom of England","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Welsh_Marches","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Norman invasion of Wales","from":1067,"to":1283,"outcome":"The Norman invasion 1067-1081 and the stronger invasion from 1081; Welsh recovery during the Anarchy (1135-1154); Henry II took homage from Rhys ap Gruffydd and Owain Gwynedd in 1163; ended by Edward I's conquest.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_invasion_of_Wales"},{"name":"Glyndwr Rising","from":1400,"to":1415,"outcome":"Owain held most of Wales 1404-1408; Aberystwyth regained by 1408, Harlech in winter 1408-1409.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r"}],"certainty":[{"from":1071,"